ven-names></name><name><surname>Goldenberg</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffman</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cliver</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Brumfield</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fetal biparietal diameter, head circumference, abdominal circumference and femur length. A comparison by race and sex</article-title><source>J Reprod Med</source><year>1993</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>206</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8487238</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jacquemyn</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Sys</surname><given-names>SU</given-names></name><name><surname>Verdonk</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fetal transverse cerebellar diameter in different ethnic groups</article-title><source>J Perinat Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>14</fpage><lpage>19</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10765509</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moon</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Cho</surname><given-names>JY</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>YM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>YH</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>MY</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Nasal bone length at 11-14 weeks of pregnancy in the Korean population</article-title><source>Prenat Diagn</source><year>2006</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>524</fpage><lpage>527</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16634117</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bronshtein</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiner</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Abramovici</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Filmar</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Erlik</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Blumenfeld</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prenatal diagnosis of gall bladder anomalies-report of 17 cases</article-title><source>Prenat Diagn</source><year>1993</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>851</fpage><lpage>861</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8278315</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duchatel</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Muller</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Oury</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Mennesson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Boue</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Boue</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prenatal diagnosis of cystic fibrosis: ultrasonography of the gallbladder at 17-19 weeks of gestation</article-title><source>Fetal Diagn Ther</source><year>1993</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>28</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8452646</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hertzberg</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kliewer</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Maynor</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>McNally</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowie</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kay</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Nonvisualization of the fetal gallbladder: frequency and prognostic importance</article-title><source>Radiology</source><year>1996</year><volume>199</volume><fpage>679</fpage><lpage>682</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8637986</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Senoh</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hata</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Is there a human fetal gallbladder contractility during pregnancy?</article-title><source>Hum Reprod</source><year>2000</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>1400</fpage><lpage>1402</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10831577</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>Sonogram demonstrating fetal gall bladder length and width <bold>(A)</bold> and height <bold>(B)</bold>. The height was obtained by rotating the transducer 90 degree from plane <bold>(A)</bold> showing maximal length and width of the gall bladder. The caliper placement for measurement of the gall bladder is demonstrated. S = spine, B = bladder</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-54-g001"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>Visualization rate of the fetal gall bladder according to gestational age.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-54-g002"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Fetal Gall Bladder Length, Height, Width, Area and Volume according to Gestational Age</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-54-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-Data are mean &#x000b1; standard deviation.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Pearson Correlation Coefficients between Measured Parameters and Gestational Age</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-54-i002"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Reference Values of Fetal Gall Bladder Length and Area according to Gestational Age</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-54-i003"/></table-wrap></floats-group></article>